<title>USA: U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. upland cotton major sales activity in the week ended Oct 3 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in 1,000 running bales:</p>
<p> Net Sales:   1996/97	   1997/98</p>
<p>  Mexico	74,200		Nil</p>
<p>  Turkey	44,000</p>
<p>  South Korea 21,400</p>
<p>  Japan	 16,200</p>
<p>  Indonesia   15,000</p>
<p>Net sales of 198,000 running bales were up 78 percent from the previous week and exceed the four-week average by 73 percent.</p>
<p>Weekly exports of 36,400 running bales were one-third lower than the previous week and 22 percent below the four-week average.</p>
<p>Asian destinations accounted for 42 percent of the weeks shipments, Western Hemisphere 44 percent, Africa 11 percent and Europe three percent.</p>
</text>
